 "files": [
  {
   "sha": "be3641f8c338fd3db4aab8ef420a016fc835b577",
   "filename": "docs/streams/upgrade-guide.md",
   "status": "modified",
   "additions": 3,
   "deletions": 1,
   "changes": 4,
   "blob_url": "https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/9a17bbb285a4259f0e0d69a780da7727f637243b/docs%2Fstreams%2Fupgrade-guide.md",
   "raw_url": "https://github.com/apache/kafka/raw/9a17bbb285a4259f0e0d69a780da7727f637243b/docs%2Fstreams%2Fupgrade-guide.md",
   "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/kafka/contents/docs%2Fstreams%2Fupgrade-guide.md?ref=9a17bbb285a4259f0e0d69a780da7727f637243b",
   "patch": "@@ -65,10 +65,12 @@ Starting in Kafka Streams 2.6.x, a new processing mode is available, named EOS v\n \n Since 2.6.0 release, Kafka Streams depends on a RocksDB version that requires MacOS 10.14 or higher.\n \n-## Streams API changes in 4.3.0\n+## Streams API changes in 4.3.2\n \n Processors returning the same `StoreBuilder` instance from `ConnectedStoreProvider#stores()` are now grouped into one subtopology ([KAFKA-20464](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20464)). For affected applications, task IDs change and state is restored from the changelog on first startup after upgrading. Linking processors to a store by name is unaffected.\n \n+## Streams API changes in 4.3.0\n+\n **Note:** Kafka Streams 4.3.0 contains a critical native memory leak in the RocksDB state store layer ([KAFKA-20616](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20616)). The `ColumnFamilyOptions` for the offsets column family is not closed, and column family handles can leak on close-path exceptions, which under cascading task closes (e.g., rebalances or error-triggered recoveries) leads to unbounded off-heap memory growth and eventual OOM. Users running Kafka Streams should consider upgrading directly to 4.3.1, which includes the fix for it.\n \n Kafka Streams now supports `ProcessingExceptionHandler` for global store/KTable processing via [KIP-1270](https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1270%3A+Extend+ProcessExceptionalHandler+for+GlobalThread). Previously, the `ProcessingExceptionHandler` only applied to regular stream tasks. With this release, you can now configure exception handling for global store/KTables by setting the new config `processing.exception.handler.global.enabled` to `true` (recommended). When enabled, the configured `ProcessingExceptionHandler` will be invoked for exceptions occurring during global store/KTable processing. Note that Dead Letter Queue (DLQ) support is not yet available for global store/KTable and will be added in an upcoming release. More details can be found in [KIP-1270](https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1270%3A+Extend+ProcessExceptionalHandler+for+GlobalThread)."
  }
 ],
